{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/54324-tell-me-about-the-trinity-continuum","id":54324,"title":"Tell me about the Trinity Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-20T16:50:26-08:00","id":54324,"title":"Tell me about the Trinity Continuum","content":"So, I have Adventure! and I really like the setting, but I never got into the other two iterations of the game. Would anyone like to give me a quick overview of them? I know there will be changes with the new editions, but I figure the games will still have similar broad strokes.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious how they link up and all that.<br /> <br /> Why do people like the other two settings?<br /> <br /> All that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T23:45:48-08:00","id":54508,"title":"","content":"<br /> In Aberrant 1e, the explosion of the space station Galatea in 1999 triggered the eruption of novas (the setting's term for superhumans) worldwide. The game's starting point is set 9 years after that, the novas' presence already having shaped societies considerably.<br /> <br /> (Well, that's what everyone thinks happened. The truth is, the Galatea explosion was a side-effect. A certain Doctor Primoris manipulated the fundamental forces of the universe to create more superhumans like himself; he's better known in this era as Divas Mal.)<br /> <br /> You're one of the novas, a celebrity, a superstar, someone with the potential to change the world. What are you going to do with that power?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Canonically, over time, the novas became drunk on their power, grew corrupted, twisted, insane, renamed Aberrants. Eventually, things came to a head in the Aberrant War, humanity fighting those they had once called heroes. The war ended with the Aberrants departing for deep space, having been given the choice of exile or destruction of the planet.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Aeon / Trinity is set in the 2120s. The world is recovering from the Aberrant War, some places better than others. Now, however... the Aberrants are back, to reclaim their homeworld.<br /> <br /> You're a psion, someone who's been gifted with extraordinary psychic abilities to stand against the threat of the Aberrants, and to help put the world back together.<br /> <br /> Want a sci-fi genre? The 2120s can provide. Cyberpunk? North America. After the end? Europe. Military sci-fi? Australia. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T06:55:10-08:00","id":54634,"title":"","content":"As marin noted, \u00c6on provides a hodgepodge milieu against a larger backdrop of space opera. Aberrant is much more about the examination of celebrity culture and hero worship through the lens of tights- wearing superheroes (and a realistic take on &quot;what if heroes were real&quot;). Adventure! is, of course, hero pulps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:37:09-08:00","id":54725,"title":"","content":"The links between the games are loose, and optional depending on what kind of game you want to run.<br /> <br /> Some elements from <b>Adventure!</b> are &quot;prequel&quot; appearances for <b>Aberrant</b> and <b>Trinity</b> - Max Mercer and Michael Donighal / Dr. Primoris / Divis Mal are among the key figures of the setting, but Mal is the only one &quot;on stage&quot; in <b>Aberrant</b>.<br /> <br /> A lot of the weirder pulp action stuff in <b>Adventure!</b> fades out as the Z-waves go (so there are no lost cities or intelligent apes in <b>Aberrant</b> as written, for example) because each game is essentially a different genre or set of genres.<br /> <br /> 2008 and 2120 are the canon future of the setting, but not necessarily the only one. After all, Max is a time traveller...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:09:59-08:00","id":55203,"title":"","content":"Neat. Do they actually explain what happened to all the intelligent Apes and Pulp Heroes after the 50s and 60s? I mean, I totally understand that Aberrant is operating on a different set of tropes and stuff, but if they're gonna connect the settings, I'd enjoy knowing where all the old heroes went.<br /> <br /> ...Also, in AEon, is anyone worried about the psions eventually going power mad? I get that, if you're defending against the Magneto and the Brotherhood of Evil Space Mutants, you need some oomph on your side, but I'd think that people would be somewhat untrustworthy of psions.<br /> <br /> What's actually the difference between an Aberrant and a Psion? Do Psions get get the manipulate the mind type mentalism powers, while Aberrants get more physical transformations and direct manipulation of the world?<br /> <br /> Regardless, they both sound interesting. I'll definitely be looking into the games as they come out.<br /> <br /> ...Oh yeah. Brandon Sanderson recently started a series of books where the premise is basically &quot;What if only supervillains started showing up?&quot; The first book is Steelheart, but there's also a short story that takes place between that book and the next one that'll be coming out this fall sometime. It's pretty good and it seems like it might serve as nice inspiration for a game set during the Aberrant War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T00:17:32-08:00","id":55304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/54324-tell-me-about-the-trinity-continuum?p=55203#post55203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. Do they actually explain what happened to all the intelligent Apes and Pulp Heroes after the 50s and 60s? I mean, I totally understand that Aberrant is operating on a different set of tropes and stuff, but if they're gonna connect the settings, I'd enjoy knowing where all the old heroes went.</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, as the Z-waves faded, so did the weirdness. It's implied here and there that there were a handful of Inspired still running around, mostly staying off the radar until things pick back up in time for Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/54324-tell-me-about-the-trinity-continuum?p=55203#post55203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Also, in AEon, is anyone worried about the psions eventually going power mad? I get that, if you're defending against the Magneto and the Brotherhood of Evil Space Mutants, you need some oomph on your side, but I'd think that people would be somewhat untrustworthy of psions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of individuals are concerned about that, notably the Federated States of America. (And given that one of the leaders of the Psi Orders is head of one of the biggest corporations in the solar system, some are paranoid they're already power mad and nobody's caught on yet.) But for the most part humanity trusts them more than it distrusts them (partially because at worst they're the lesser evil, and they seem to be individually less powerful). Also, it helps a bit that Nova/Aberrant madness was known to be linked to the rise in Taint mutations over time, and Taint doesn't accumulate in Psions like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/54324-tell-me-about-the-trinity-continuum?p=55203#post55203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's actually the difference between an Aberrant and a Psion? Do Psions get get the manipulate the mind type mentalism powers, while Aberrants get more physical transformations and direct manipulation of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer: They manipulate different forces but can accomplish many of the same effects in those ways. Psions manipulate psi, and Novas/Aberrants manipulate quantum. <br /> <br /> Long answer: Both have ways of interacting with the world, but Nova/Aberrant powers do tend to be a lot more direct with a good deal of sheer bang for one's buck, power-wise. They operate at something of a cost, as Novas/Aberrants are prone to mutations and insanity as their power grows and they channel more and more of it. Psions, however, seem to be more common but are generally more low-key in terms of raw strength but their abilities come at at much lower risk to the user. Novas/Aberrants can put out a lot more raw power, actually transforming energy and physical matter at the molecular level and what have you, but Psions have much more subtle advantages. A Psion clairvoyant or teleporter, for instance, is limited more by the ability to conceptualize the target than by range. Psions also have access to biotech, which is more compatible with their bodies and abilities than it is with Novas/Aberrants (I believe Aberrants can't use biotech at all, as their bodies are attuned to quantum energies rather than psionic ones). The mechanism for this is never really explained, but when you get psi and quantum energies in the lower, more balanced levels seen in Adventure! you get the Z-wave effect but if things lean too much in one direction they start contrasting and interfering with each other.<br /> <br /> To put it in Adventure! terms, Stalwarts are the precursors to the Novas eventually activated in the late 90's. Mesmerists are precursors to the Psions. Both types are capable of a lot of overlap in terms of basic abilities (which is why there is a common house rule for Adventure! that Stalwarts and Mesmerists can purchase each others' Knacks as if they were a level higher).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T04:08:39-08:00","id":61450,"title":"","content":"Another thing that made the intelligent apes and other weirdness disappear is that Aeon started erasing all records of them and spinning a disinformation campaign sometime in the '30s or '40s so by the '50 or so only the tabloids would consider publishing anything much about them. Some of the Aberrant fluff mentions a hidden repository of newspaper articles of weird events that someone found and had to be erased (of course by this time Proteus is a very nasty black ops agency with a lot of power and it is implied that they silenced the discovering party permanently).<br /> <br /> Disinformation and suppression of information is also present in the Aeon Trinity era, a good example of which is the fact that Novas fought the Aberrants along side of the baseline humans and that there are still sane Novas out it space. The prevalent belief around 2120 is that all of the Novas of the early 21st century became twisted insane monsters though some, like the teleporters who have encountered some of the sane Novas know better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:35:15-07:00","id":94504,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Not-So Scientific Treatise on the Comparisons of Daredevils/Mesmerists/Stalwarts, Novas/Aberrants, and Psiads/Psions</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(TL;DR toward the bottom, since this turned out to be very long)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, I\u2019ve noticed that some people occasionally have difficulty understanding the difference between the \u201clesser\u201d Inspired, Novas/Aberrants, and Psiads/Psions. This is totally understandable, since the VAST majority of information provided on the nature of the Inspired is provided in the context of in-world and in-character discoveries and knowledge -- and the inhabitants of the Aeonverse don\u2019t understand Inspiration that much!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To try to remedy this dearth of data, I\u2019m going to give a few analogies that I\u2019ve occasionally used to help my players understand the similarities and differences between people who use Telluric, Quantum, and Noetic energies. Like any analogy, these aren\u2019t PERFECT (they get muddy if you try to think about how a Mesmerist summons up fire or ice, things like that), but they do a fairly good job on the whole of it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the first analogy, let\u2019s imagine a very basic problem: there\u2019s a big-*** boulder that needs to be moved from Point A to Point B. The distance between the two points is arbitrary (far enough that it would cause problems) and the exact weight/mass of the boulder is arbitrary (large enough that it would cause problems). Under normal circumstances, an average human being would find that this boulder is far too large to move without mechanical aid -- they\u2019d need to bring in construction equipment or the like to move it. Now, in addition to our normal human (or \u201cbaseline\u201d, if you will), let\u2019s imagine five additional people: a Daredevil/Talent, a Mesmerist, a Stalwart, a Nova/Aberrant, and a Psiad/Psion. These five people each have some trick which allows them to move the boulder without relying on heavy machinery. Egads! How is this possible?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If our normal human were to observe these five individuals, all five appear to do identical things: they walk up to the boulder, push on it with their arms, and the boulder moves. From an objective, universal Point Of View, however, these people are doing VERY different things. Let\u2019s begin with the analogy proper!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Imagine, if you will, that the universe is a computer -- identical in many respects to the desktop on which you are probably browsing this forum. We can roughly divide this universal computer into three parts:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- the INPUT (the keyboard, mouse, joystick, trackpad, Wacom, Leap Motion, whathaveyou) which accepts input and data for processing and manipulation; for our universe, this would represent any actions a person performs or any natural event which occurs</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- the OPERATING SYSTEM (Windows, Mac OS, Linux, any specific programs you\u2019re using) which tell the computer how to interpret and manipulate data; for our universe, this would be Newtonian Physics, Quantum Mechanics, and other Laws of Nature, which determine how things interact and how Cause leads to Effect</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- the OUTPUT (monitor, speakers, etc) which takes the processed input and data, and displays the results; for our universe, this would be anything which we observe as having resulted from an action or event</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In this analogy, the act of starting a fire would be as follows: a heat source is the INPUT, the OPERATING SYSTEM (Laws of Nature) say that the energy in the pile of wood is now high enough to spontaneously combust with oxygen, and the OUTPUT is a now-burning pile of wood.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Let\u2019s return to our five Inspired individuals (and our single confused and probably awed normal human). Despite the fact that they all managed the same feat, they arrived at it in vastly different manners. Breaking them down one-by-one, we can see how each of them manipulate the universe to pull off superhuman feats. Daredevils/Talents, Mesmerists, and Stalwarts all have abilities which increase their capabilities (mechanically, this is usually represented by increase the number of dice or successes for certain tasks). Novas/Aberrants and Psiads/Psions have more obviously supernatural powers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- The Daredevil/Talent has an incredible amount of training and luck, granting him better chances and skill at moving the rock (with Ability Mastery: Might and a point of Inspiration to double his dice pool, he gets radically more successes than our normal human)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- The Mesmerist has an almost mind-over-matter control of his body\u2019s natural processes, and can grant himself hysterical strength (with the right Knack, he might be able to add Willpower to feats of raw strength for a short while if he pushes himself)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- The Stalwart is a quintessential strong-man, and his muscles are powerful enough to put The Governator to shame (with the right Knack, he could add his Destructive Facet to any feats of strength)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Looking at these three, they all have a similar theme. Can you notice it? In order to perform a feat that most humans couldn\u2019t manage, they all manipulated some aspect of the universe -- for these \u201clesser\u201d Inspired, they lack the raw power to change most things, but there is one thing they can manipulate: the INPUT. They can all change the raw INPUT into the universe before that information/cause/effort is processed (represented by the fact that Telluric Energy is pretty good at adding dice to their dice pools for actions). A higher INPUT (effort) means that the OPERATING SYSTEM (universe) spits out an improved OUTPUT (result), and the boulder moves. In order to get the right OUTPUT on the \u201cscreen\u201d of the universe, they worked harder to put in more INPUT through the keyboard and mouse, giving the OPERATING SYSTEM more to work with.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How about the Psiad/Psion?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- The Psiad/Psion has a significant leg-up from our previous Inspired; they can manipulate Noetic Energy. Using Noetic Energy, our Psiad/Psion changes how the boulder\u2019s matter interacts with the universe via the Higgs mechanism; in doing so, the gravitational and inertial mass of the boulder is changed, making it weigh less, which makes it easy enough for our Psiad/Psion\u2019s normal muscles to move it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now we\u2019ve got something different on our hands. In this instance, we can see that the Psiad/Psion is not really that much stronger than most people, but they still moved the boulder. They didn\u2019t make themselves stronger, but they didn\u2019t actually make the boulder lighter -- they didn\u2019t change the informational content of the boulder; instead, they changed how the universe INTERPRETED the informational content of the boulder. They used Noetic Energy to affect the OPERATING SYSTEM of the universe, temporarily changing how physics and the Laws of Nature worked. They kept the INPUT the same, but changed how the OPERATING SYSTEM used that INPUT in order to affect the OUTPUT indirectly. Obviously, this gives Psiads/Psions a great benefit; they can perform an enormous variety of actions that would be beyond the reach of even the most capable human, by stretching and pulling how the universe operates, allowing the impossible to temporarily become possible. In order to get the right OUTPUT on the \u201cscreen\u201d of the universe, they did not change how much INPUT they gave through the keyboard or mouse, but instead changed how the OPERATING SYSTEM used what little they could give it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finally, let\u2019s take a look at the Nova/Aberrant.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--- The Nova/Aberrant can manipulate Quantum Energy. Using Quantum Energy, our Nova/Aberrant does not increase their muscle mass, or supplement their training, or alter the boulder\u2019s mass. Instead, they push the massive boulder with (more-or-less) normal human muscles, and the boulder just MOVES.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What the frack? How did that work? Our particular Nova/Aberrant doesn\u2019t have superdense muscles or Olympian training, so they\u2019re technically just as strong as our normal human. They didn\u2019t change the mass of the boulder, either, so they\u2019re pushing with normal human muscles on a (literally) massive boulder. But it still moved! Basic kinematics (the OPERATING SYSTEM) tells us that shouldn\u2019t have happened with such relatively little force (the INPUT). It worked, because our Nova/Aberrant\u2019s manipulation of Quantum Energies simply MADE IT MOVE -- they changed the OUTPUT directly, without manipulating either the INPUT or the OPERATING SYSTEM. Novas break the rules -- really, they do. They need not concern themselves with what they themselves are capable of doing (the INPUT) or what the universe is normally capable of doing (the OPERATING SYSTEM). In order to get the right OUTPUT on the \u201cscreen\u201d of the universe, they just straight-up ignored their regular INPUT through the keyboard and mouse, and the OPERATING SYSTEM of the computer -- all they do is will the right pixels to light up and vibrations for the speakers, and they make whatever they want happen. Terrifying, really, when you think about it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(TL;DR begins here) For a much more simplified version of this, we can just boil all of that down to a mathematical equation: it has an input/variable (the effort you put into an action), a constant (the physical laws of the universe), and the output/result of the equation (what you see as the result of your actions).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For simplicity\u2019s sake, let\u2019s say it is (2)*X = Y for our purposes. For whatever superhuman feat you need to perform, Y MUST equal 8, for completely arbitrary purposes. To do whatever it is you want to do, you need to put in 4 units of\u2026 whatever. Less than 4, nothing happens -- you don\u2019t measure up to what the universe says is necessary. Normally, however, a human being is only capable of putting in 2 units of whatever. Uh-oh! How do our Inspired examples fix this?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Our Daredevil and his friends use Telluric Energy to manipulate the input they can give -- normally, the most a human can make X equal is 2, but the Daredevil can get a bit more oomph out of himself, and he can make X equal 4. Plug this in, and we get the following:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(2)*4 = 8</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fantastic! It works.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Our Psiad/Psion can\u2019t do more than the average human -- their X can only be as high as 2 -- but they CAN use Noetic Energy to change the universal constants involved, so they change the constant from (2) to (4). Plug this in, and we get the following:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(4)*2 = 8</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wunderbar! We can still make it work.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, the Nova/Aberrant. They don\u2019t put in more effort (X = 2), and they don\u2019t change the universal constants [(2) will still equal (2)], but they can directly manipulate the output Y and simply overwrite what the universe SAYS it should be with what they WANT it to be. So, we get the following:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(2)*2 = 8</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This makes absolutely no sense, which is exactly why Novas and Aberrants terrify people in the Aeonverse -- they can do, literally, ANYTHING THEY WANT. They are in no shape or form inhibited by human limitations or universal constants. Law of Conservation of Energy? Only for wusses. Speed of Light? More of a suggestion, really.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So. That was much longer than I planned. I hope that makes sense.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":".  Edited for better formatting 03-19-2014, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T13:38:47-07:00","id":95183,"title":"","content":"I suppose I should also point out that, according to many sources, &quot;Telluric Energy&quot; isn't actually a real energy at all; Mesmerists and Stalwarts don't both manipulate &quot;Telluric Energy&quot;. Instead, it is suggested that Mesmerists manipulate low-level Noetic Energy, and Stalwarts manipulate low-level Quantum Energy. In my game, I noted the the problems that this could cause -- namely, there are instances in which the energies manipulated by both Mesmerists and Stalwarts could be used to the same goal, such as having a person of each type of Inspiration fueling the same Telluric Battery. If they really were combining both Noetic and Quantum Energies, they should be canceling each other out (or otherwise reaction/neutralizing) instead of compounding their effects.<br /> <br /> To that end, I use the interpretation which states that Telluric Energy is distinct from Noetic and Quantum Energies, and it is the same energy used by Mesmerists, Stalwarts, and (passively) by Daredevils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T10:46:17-07:00","id":96411,"title":"","content":"I have Gm'd all three settings, trinity is my favorite for numerous reason ( my highlevel of default sci-fi geekery being one). What really got me into the the setting where the pregenned adventures. The Darkness revealed' trilogy and the the alien encounters adventures where very well written, each one expanded the universe with setting, people and tools as well as giving a story that put the PCs at the center of unfolding events. letting them fight the aberrant, polotics with aliens,, save the earth and lower martian real-estate values in a fashion that really helped make it easy to make them feel part of the world. (which they could save or seriously screw up) T","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2567-joedylan","name":"Joedylan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T11:01:15-07:00","id":96422,"title":"","content":"Another key diffrence is that there are two kinds of human psi user. Psychomorphs as mentioned in aberrant players guide are ' natural' psions able to develop a wide array of psychic talents. in the 2120's these are generally NOT known about. Most psychics are made by taking a human with 'potential and putting them in the ' Prometheus chamber. ( dunking them in a tank) Psions made way are strong only in a single discipline of psiontics ( telekinesis, telepathy etc ) but they develop it much easier than a psychomorph could. One Psi discipline &quot; quantakinesis' the ability to manipulate nova energies with psi powers, is only availible to psions, and another 'teleportation' is availbile at a much higher level to psions. ( psychmorphs can teleport themselves, a Teleporter psion of sufficent strengh can rip a swirly gate in the fabric of the universe big enough to send a space fleet on an intersteller voyge). Unbeknownst to most the tech of the Prometheus chambers and humans new biotech is a 'gift' from mysterious alien benefactors with an agenda. These aliens arranged for the quantakinetic discipline to be driven to extinction when the quantakinetics started finding ways of 'curing' aberrations and making nova sane, rather than working to wipe them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2567-joedylan","name":"Joedylan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T16:26:08-07:00","id":96575,"title":"","content":"Just going to second Joedylan's Trinity love. <br /> <br /> Trinity ('Aeon') is my all time fave game to GM and I have collected pretty much everything for the line several times over. <br /> <br /> Trinity has epic scifi while still being largely 'solar system' grounded, post apocalyptic dystopias, amazing biotechnology, aforementioned Psions that, in the old edition at least, had to figure out how to work together to take down the bad guys instead of relying purely on powers and so much more. Its worth picking up the Trinity Rulebook at drivethrurpg.com, its less than $10 and is a great read.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Trinity adventure books, I'm just in the process (like this weekend) of wrapping up GMing the Alien Encounter: Invasion book, which has the culmination of the storyline in the Darkness Revealed Trilogy Joedylan mentioned. Sure, they need a tweak here and there but as pre-written stories go Darkness Revelead and the Alien Encounter books are some of the best I've GM'd. This would be the second time I've run through the DR related stories in full now, come to think of it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Trinity for the win <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Having said that..... we're talking about the Trinity Universe above, not the Trinity Continuum. The Continuum is the reboot that hasn't been released yet, and it'll be different in places so what you see in Trinity (or Aberrant or Adventure!) original edition and won't necessarily be the same in the Continuum version....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T17:33:42-07:00","id":96602,"title":"","content":"One of the first core elements that I remember reading about that not just hooked me on to Aberrant, Trinity, and Adventure! (the ! is very important, just a note) and then the whole saga of White Wolf books itself was the character of Divis Mal. We share a common trait (and while I wish it was cool quantum powers, it is sadly not) which called to me and made me want to know more and more and more about him and the settign that he was in, and the company that produced said character and setting. From that I found the World of Darkness, Exalted, and all sorts of other concepts.<br /> <br /> What kept me in love with the setting was how intrinicate it was, how the three parts fit together as a whole, and that the elements in Adventure! set the stage for the activities in both Aberrant and Trinity. My huge love of pulp action, superhero saga, and scifi were combined into one glorious setting that touched upon it all.<br /> <br /> Especially in Trinity, with the Psions and the Orders and the space travel, colony exploration. Made even richer when the book about Eden novas (yes, novas, not aberrants, its very important, hehe) were read by me.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this helps any, but the fact that the setting is collective makes the whole the interesting, and the messages that follow on each story is also pretty inspirational. The fact that its getting a remake has me really happy, I think the setting and the game mechanics need some love.<br /> <br /> As a final note to add - though I have ran D&amp;D games, and Exalted game, the games that I remember the fondness was my Aberrant game, which lasted for about a year of school time and had the theme of novas being hired to explore parallel worlds, it was great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T21:31:56-07:00","id":96709,"title":"","content":"Do you both have arms, LordHeru? There's no shame in having arms, you know...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T12:45:14-07:00","id":96996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/54324-tell-me-about-the-trinity-continuum?p=96709#post96709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you both have arms, LordHeru? There's no shame in having arms, you know...</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha. Oh man, I haven't heard that in the longest time. It brings back memories of the time when there was constant debates, discussions, and creations related to this setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}